OpenRouter models from other vendors now get yoagent's real vendor limits instead of the 128K window and 4096-token reply cap. Committed as 4bd66c7c, marked Part of #1122. Build, the full test suite, clippy, fmt and tests/harness_logic.sh all pass.

The change: if yoyo's own Anthropic mapping finds nothing, the OpenRouter branch in create_model_config (src/agent_builder.rs) now asks yoagent's ModelConfig::preset("openrouter", model). It copies only the context window, max output tokens and reasoning flag, so:
• the URL stays yoyo's, and a user's --base-url still wins over the URL yoagent hardcodes;
• client headers are still added the same way;
• cost is untouched.

yoyo's Anthropic mapping still runs first because yoagent rejects the dashed ids existing configs use (anthropic/claude-sonnet-4-6, anthropic/claude-opus-5-5), and its rows carry no price.

Before and after, on the built binary (`-p hi` against a dead URL, so nothing was sent):

| id | before | after |
|---|---|---|
| google/gemini-3.6-flash, google/gemini-3.8-flash | warned, 128K / 4096 | no warning, 1048576 / 65536 |
| x-ai/grok-4.7 | warned | no warning, 500000 / 64000 |
| openai/gpt-6-sol | warned | no warning, 1050000 / 64000 |
| openai/gpt-6, meta-llama/llama-4, anthropic/claude-sonnet-4.6:batch | warned | still warn (yoagent has no row for them) |
| dotted and dashed Anthropic ids | no warning | no warning, same as before |

Tests (src/openrouter_preset_tests.rs):
• The expected limits are read from yoagent's routed preset and checked against the vendor's own preset, rather than typed in by hand. A custom --base-url case confirms the user's URL survives.
• A second test pins the dashed Anthropic ids as the places where yoagent and yoyo disagree.
• One existing test changed on purpose: openai/gpt-6-sol moved off the "still guesses" list because it now has real limits. openai/gpt-6, meta-llama/llama-4 and the 4.6 :batch id were added to that list.
• I broke the new lookup on purpose and the new test failed by name; with the code restored it passes.

Pricing: unchanged by this diff, because /cost uses yoyo's own price table with the vendor prefix stripped (format/cost.rs:82). While checking it I found two things, now posted on #1012:
• anthropic/claude-sonnet-4.6:batch is billed at full price, but OpenRouter charges half for :batch, so /cost shows double.
• gemini-3.8-flash costs the same as 3.6-flash in that table, which may be wrong.

Other: src/agent_builder.rs grew by 4 lines, so I raised its size limit in tests/module_size.rs from 4977 to 4981 with a note. docs/src/configuration/models.md now explains which OpenRouter ids get vendor limits.

Tickets:
• #1122: comment listing the ids where the two lookups disagree, which is why yoyo's Anthropic mapping can't be deleted.
• #1117: comment saying it stays open, because yoagent has no rows for those Anthropic ids either.
• #1012: the two pricing findings above.
